The body-sensitivity and non-vacuity gates both behaved correctly. Changing the submitted body’s base from `2` to `3` produced `3` at `(1,5)` and made the unchanged claim for `2` fail with a stuck configuration. Independently, an off-by-one result mutation built successfully but failed with the expected implication residual (`powmod + 1 = powmod` was unmet).
Mode integrity, source fidelity, differential testing, clean concrete/proof reconstruction, isolated positive claims, body sensitivity, and fresh non-vacuity have all been executed with preserved logs. The remaining work is the exhaustive written soundness/trust accounting and final verdict.
