codex
The static audit found a domain-sensitive modeling limitation worth preserving: the K `^%Int` hook uses truncating remainder, while Python’s three-argument `pow` follows Python’s modulus sign. They agree throughout the claimed `p > 0` domain, but for `(2,-5)` K returns `4` and Python returns `-1`. I will treat this as an over-broad generated-semantics limitation outside the formal theorem, not as an on-domain false-proof witness.
apply patch
